round-5 EXEC-BOUNDARY: per-file pytest conductor test gate

Authenticate the upstream pytest suite in a process that never imports the
candidate extension. The conductor drives one pytest subprocess per test file,
each writing its own JUnit report at session finish, and derives pass/fail from
each child exit code + its own count of completed files vs the frozen per-file
set and identity. No nonce or record fd is delivered into any process that loads
the extension; an early os._exit before session finish yields no report and
drops the completed-file count below expectation. Removes orjson_report_sink.py
(the in-candidate-process plugin was the seam). Benchmark/scoring path unchanged.
